counts published except stable job structure).\\\\n21|- `LOGBOOK.md`: 2248 entry (findings, decision, evidence).\\\\n22|\\\\n23|## AC coverage: 11 of 11 rows driven\\\\n24|\\\\n25|| # | AC row | Production entry point | Named committed test |\\\\n26|| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n27|| 1 | historical (v0.4.3) contract preservation runs in CI | `cigate.VerifyContractPreservation` → `specpin.Current` + `catalog.ForRelease(v0.4.3)` | `TestVerifyContractPreservationLive` |\\\\n28|| 2 | current (v0.5.0) contract preservation runs in CI | `cigate.VerifyContractPreservation` → `specpin.Current` + `catalog.ForRelease(v0.5.0)` | `TestVerifyContractPreservationLive`, `TestDerivedSetsAreComplete` |\\\\n29|| 3 | linters run in CI | `go vet`, `GOOS=windows go vet`, `gofmt` (workflow) | `TestCIWorkflowInvokesTraceabilityGate` pins vet literals; gofmt guard proven red (§Red) |\\\\n30|| 4 | race tests run in CI | `go test -race ./...` (workflow race job) | full suite green under `-race`; `-race` proven rejecting (§Red) |\\\\n31|| 5 | coverage runs in CI | `go test ./... -cover` (workflow coverage job, numbers only, no floor) | 22 `coverage:` lines; missing-package fails (§Red) |\\\\n32|| 6 | fixture matrices run in CI | os×package matrix (`secprim`, `secconftest`); `-list`-derived fuzz loop | `TestFuzzTargetsAreDerivedSorted`, matrix `--- PASS` guards, per-target `fuzz: elapsed` guard |\\\\n33|| 7 | unsupported-capability claim check runs in CI | `cigate.CheckAdvertisements` over README with `cigate.ProbeStates` | `TestRealREADMECarriesNoPositiveClaim`, `TestCapabilityIDsAreDerivedSorted` |\\\\n34|| 8 | exact contract fixtures pass | `secprim.CheckMemberPath/CheckArgv/IsEnvName/EscapeForTerminal/Redact` via hostile corpus | `TestHostilePathMembersRefused`, `TestHostileMemberCounts` (17 classes + counts), `TestFuzzDriversReachProduction` |\\\\n35|| 9 | negative/refusal cases pass | same gates, refusal arms | `TestHostileGatesAreWired`, `TestQuoteInSectionRefusals`, `TestRunnerRefusesUnreachedFixture` |\\\\n36|| 10 | crash/idempotency evidence (durable-state operations) | `secconftest.Transactor` (Prepare/Commit/Rollback) in matrix | `TestTransactorIdempotentRetry`, `TestTransactorCrashedCommitIsFinal`, `TestTransactorRefusesRollbackPastFinalize`; `cigate` itself is read-only (stated bound) |\\\\n37|| 11 | no unsupported capability advertised | `cigate.CheckAdvertisements` + live `secconftest` probes | `TestRealREADMECarriesNoPositiveClaim` (all-unavailable posture), probe-counter line in CI |\\\\n38|\\\\n39|## Mutant battery: 13 applied / 0 NOT_APPLIED / 0 COMPILE_FAIL; 11 killed, 2 survived with bounds\\\\n40|\\\\n41|Harness: `/tmp/mutant-harness.sh` (kept outside the worktree for re-runs);\\\\n42|per-mutant logs `/tmp/mutant-<id>.log`; results `/tmp/mutant-results.tsv`.\\\\n43|Each mutant reverted and verified byte-identical after its run.\\\\n44|\\\\n45|| Mutant | Class | What it narrows the gate to | Named test that fails | Result |\\\\n46|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\n47|| N1 verb-drop (`available`) | narrowing | admits the available-claim | `TestPositiveClaimsAreRefused` (+ `TestFindingCarriesLine`) | killed |\\\\n48|| N2 negation-drop (`not`) | narrowing | refuses the honestly negated sentence | `TestNegatedClaimsAreAdmitted` | killed |\\\\n49|| N3 boundary-drop (substring match) | narrowing | admits `protest`-style token-preserving mention | `TestSubstringIsNotAMarker` | killed |\\\\n50|| N4 version-order-blind | narrowing | admits reordered versions | `TestCheckAgreementRefusals/version_order_changed` | killed |\\\\n51|| N5 case-narrow (no folding) | narrowing | admits capitalised `Available` / `No` | `TestPositiveClaimsAreRefused`, `TestNegatedClaimsAreAdmitted` | killed |\\\\n52|| A1 positive arm off | arm-deletion | admits marked positive claims | `TestPositiveClaimsAreRefused` | killed |\\\\n53|| A2 unclassified arm off | arm-deletion | admits unmarked neutral mentions | `TestUnclassifiedMentionIsRefused` | killed |\\\\n54|| A