verified after all 14 reviewer mutants | `6c8e29de…` unchanged; every mutated file restored byte-identically (SHA-256 asserted, `ALL RESTORED`) |\n23|\n24|Mutants were applied to a scratch copy at `/tmp/vmzk0y-rev4-mut`, never to the\n25|candidate worktree.\n26|\n27|## Gates re-run by this reviewer\n28|\n29|| Gate | Result |\n30||---|---|\n31|| `go build ./...` | exit 0 |\n32|| `go vet ./...` | exit 0 |\n33|| `gofmt -l internal/` | clean |\n34|| `go test ./... -count=1` | exit 0, 22 packages `ok`, no FAIL |\n35|| `go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck` | ok — contracts=60, normative_sections=36, acceptance_cases=98 |\n36|\n37|Not re-run by me (stated, not implied): `GOOS=windows` build/vet, `-race`,\n38|coverage. The round-4 outcome states the same; no gate is claimed on their\n39|behalf.\n40|\n41|---\n42|\n43|## G-A — the behavioural-versus-census split: CLOSED\n44|\n45|The report exists and is **derived, not asserted**: `battery-round4.json`\n46|records a per-mutant `killed_by` list, and the BEHAVIOURAL/CENSUS category is\n47|recomputable from whether `TestDerivedRefusalArmsAreAllWitnessed` /\n48|`TestWitnessedArmsAreAllDerived` appear in it. Recomputing from the JSON\n49|reproduces the outcome table exactly: 24 rows, 22 applied / 21 KILLED /\n50|1 SURVIVED(equivalent) + 1 NOT_APPLIED + 1 COMPILE_FAIL as distinct rows;\n51|narrowing 14, narrowing/token-preserving 4, arm-deletion 2, census-only 1.\n52|\n53|**No production arm is reported as census-only** — the single census-only row\n54|(M15) mutates the census itself. So the spot-check asked for (\"two it calls\n55|census-only\") has no candidate; I spot-checked two BEHAVIOURAL-ONLY, two BOTH\n56|and the true saturation narrowing instead, running the census mask and the\n57|behavioural mask as separate processes:\n58|\n59|| Reviewer mutant | Reported | Census mask (census pair) | Behavioural mask | Verdict |\n60||---|---|---|---|---|\n61|| RM17 `if digit == ':' { continue }` inserted above the unchanged major condition | BEHAVIOURAL ONLY | exit 0, 2 RUN / 2 PASS | exit 1 — `TestParseMajorDigitBoundariesRefuseAtEntry` | matches |\n62|| RM18 `if rest[i] == '/' { continue }` inserted above the unchanged rest condition | BEHAVIOURAL ONLY | exit 0, 2 RUN / 2 PASS | exit 1 — same test | matches |\n63|| RM5 `rest[i] < '/'` (condition edit) | BOTH | exit 1 — both census tests | exit 1 — same test | matches |\n64|| RM6 `digit > ':'` (condition edit) | BOTH | exit 1 — both census tests | exit 1 — same test | matches |\n65|| RM3 `major > (MaxInt-step)/10` -> `major > MaxInt/10` | BEHAVIOURAL | exit 0 | exit 1 — `TestParseMajorSaturationEdge` alone | matches |\n66|\n67|Masks verified non-empty (2 and 236 `=== RUN` lines respectively), so no row is\n68|a silently-empty selection.\n69|\n70|## G-B — the edges: two of four sites closed\n71|\n72|Closed and re-verified:\n73|\n74|- **Saturation guard at `provhost.parseMajor`.** Largest admitted\n75|  (`9223372036854775807`), first saturated (`…808`), the aliasing witness\n76|  `922337203685477580802.0.0` and its ±1 neighbours are all driven through\n77|  `DecodeResponse` with `incompatible_protocol` / exit 6 / `observed` asserted.\n78|  RM3 confirms the guard literal cannot move by one term (killed by\n79|  `TestParseMajorSaturationEdge` alone, zero census kill).\n80|- **`/` (0x2F) and `:` (0x3A) at `parseMajor`,** in the major and in *both*\n81|  rest positions — 8 rows through `DecodeResponse` asserting\n82|  `provider_protocol_error` / exit 13 / member `protocol_version`. RM17/RM18\n83|  confirm these kills are behavioural with the condition text byte-identical.\n84|\n85|**Not done: the census of every remaining digit-range comparison in this leaf.**\n86|The round-4 battery denominator is stated as \"the nine version-classification\n87|obligations reachable from `DecodeResponse`\" — `provhost` only. Two further\n88|sites inside this leaf's delta were never censused, and both carry the shape.\n89|\n90|---\n91|\n92|## F1 (BLOCKING) — `semverMajor`'s saturation guard is pinned only far from its edge\n93|\n94|`internal/terminalbackend/terminalbackend.go:257`. The guard added by this leaf\n95|in round 2:\n96|\n97|```go\n98|if major > (math.MaxInt-digit)/10 {\n99|    return math.MaxInt\n100|}\n101|```\n102|\n103|The true narrowing — drop the `digit` term, exactly the M3/F1a shape round 4\n104|was tasked with closing at the other guard — **SURVIVES the entire\n105|terminalbackend suite**:\n106|\n107|| Reviewer mutant | Disposition | Suite |\n108||---|---|---|\n109|| S1 `major > (math.MaxInt-digit)/10` -> `major > math.MaxInt/10` | **SURVIVED** | `go test ./internal/terminalbackend/ -count=1` exit 0, 457 RUN / 457 PASS, 0 FAIL |\n110|| S2 `major > math.MaxInt` (never fires — delete-shaped) | KILLED | `TestParseProviderDescriptorProtocolVersionOverflowVectors` |\n111|\n112|So the guard's only mutant evidence is the delete-shaped one the DoD explicitly\n113|refuses (\"A delete-only mutant proves only that the gate exists\").\n114|\n115|**Measured effect at the production entry point.** Under S1,\n116|`ParseProviderDescriptor`:\n117|\n118|```\n119|PROBE semverMajor(922337203685477580801.0.0) = 1\n120|PROBE Parse(protocol_version=922337203685477580801.0.0) -> ProtocolVersion=\"922337203685477580801.0.0\" err=<nil>\n121|```\n122|\n123|A foreign protocol major is **admitted** as native major 1 — verbatim the\n124|invariant the shipped `semverMajor` doc comment asserts (\"a huge foreign major\n125|compares foreign at every `!= 1` call site rather than aliasing a small native\n126|one\"). Shipped code saturates and refuses with `descriptor protocol version`.\n127|The same aliasing reaches every `semverMajor(...) != 1` site:\n128|`terminalbackend.go:235` (`New` / `RegisterExternal`), `:556`,\n129|`manifest.go:1072`, `:1155`, `:1301`, `descriptor.go:168`.\n130|\n131|**Why the corpus misses it.** All three existing witnesses saturate under the\n132|weakened guard too — measured under S1:\n133|`semverMajor(\"18446744073709551617.0.0\") = 9223372036854775807`,\n134|`semverMajor(\"9223372036854775808.0.0\") = -9223372036854775808` (still != 1, so\n135|still refused). The guard is only ever exercised deep inside the sticky region;\n136|its edge (accumulator exactly `922337203685477580`, next digit 8 or 9) is\n137|never reached. `9223372036854775807.0.0` (largest admitted) and\n138|`9223372036854775808.0.0` (first saturated) have no rows at all.\n139|\n140|**Next round:** carry the `TestParseMajorSaturationEdge` family to\n141|`semverMajor` — largest admitted, that value plus one, and the aliasing witness\n142|`922337203685477580801.0.0` (and its ±1 neighbours) — driven through\n143|`ParseProviderDescriptor` and through one `New`/`CheckVersionTuple` call site,\n144|asserting the named refusal arm, so S1 reddens.\n145|\n146|## F2 (BLOCKING) — `descriptorGeometry`'s digit gate has no witness in the upper half of its rejected class\n147|\n148|`internal/terminalbackend/descriptor.go:235`, `if digit < '0' || digit > '9'`.\n149|This is the leaf's third digit-range comparison and was not censused.\n150|\n151|| Reviewer mutant | Disposition | Suite |\n152||---|---|---|\n153|| D0 (control) `if digit == '.' { continue }`, token-preserving | KILLED | `TestParseProviderDescriptorValueRefusals/columns_fraction`, `/rows_fraction` |\n154|| D1 `if digit == 'E' { continue }`, token-preserving | **SURVIVED** | exit 0, 457/457 PASS |\n155|| D2 `digit > '9'` -> `digit > 'E'` (bound shift) | **SURVIVED** | exit 0, 457/457 PASS |\n156|| D3 `if digit == '+' { continue }`, token-preserving | SURVIVED | equivalent — `+` is only reachable after `e`/`E`, which is refused first |\n157|\n158|The control dies, so the instrument is live.\n159|\n160|**Measured effect.** Under D2, through the production entry:\n161|\n162|```\n163|shipped: Parse(columns=1E2) -> err=...descriptor geometry digits    (correct)\n164|shipped: Parse(columns=1e2) -> err=...descriptor geometry digits    (correct)\n165|D2:      Parse(columns=1E2) -> Columns:312, err=<nil>               (admitted, fabricated)\n166|D2:      Parse(columns=1e2) -> err=...descriptor geometry digits\n167|```\n168|\n169|`1E2` is a valid JSON number naming 100; the gate admits it as **312** — a\n170|fabricated in-range value the caller cannot distinguish from a real one. That\n171|is the exact consequence class of rev1/F1, in the gate built to close rev1/F1.\n172|\n173|**Why.** `/` (0x2F) and `:` (0x3A) are unreachable through `json.Number`, so the\n174|reachable rejected class is `{-, +, ., e, E}`. The corpus witnesses `-` (`-80`),\n175|`.` (`80.0`, `24.5`) and `e` (`1e2`) — but `e` is 0x65, **44 bytes above** the\n176|true edge `'9'` (0x39). Every mutant upper bound `X` with `'E' <= X < 'e'`\n177|admits `E` and survives; `E` is the one reachable member of that 32-value\n178|window and has no row.\n179|\n180|**Next round:** add `1E2` rows on `columns` and `rows` asserting\n181|`descriptor geometry digits`, and record the census of all three digit-range\n182|comparisons in this leaf with the reachable rejected class named per site\n183|(including the declared-equivalent `/`, `:`, `+` cases), so the denominator\n184|covers the gate under review rather than provhost alone.\n185|\n186|---\n187|\n188|## Confirmed sound (re-verified by this reviewer, not read)\n189|\n190|- **Censuses fail closed**, control-planted:\n191|\n192|  | Plant | Result |\n193|  |---|---|\n194|  | Undeclared refusal arm added to `descriptor.go` production | `TestDerivedRefusalArmsAreAllDeclared` **and** `TestDeclaredRefusalArmsAreAllDerived` both FAIL |\n195|  | `var codePlantedByReviewer = \"…\"` in `internal/provider/lift.go` | `TestLiftCoversTheClosedCodeSet` FAILS |\n196|  | `const codePlantedConst = \"…\"` in a second production file of the package | `TestLiftCoversTheClosedCodeSet` FAILS |\n197|\n198|- **§7.A ownership**: `AdmitProviderDescriptor` named in `provhost/doc.go`\n199|  stated bounds and in `ownership.v0.5.0.json`; `traceability.go` review digest\n200|  re-pinned; `tracecheck` green. Both directions driven\n201|  (`TestAdmitProviderDescriptorAdmitsMatchingBinding` /\n202|  `…RefusesMismatch`, including the case-folding narrowing on generation).\n203|- **v3 envelope at provhost**: `TestDecodeResponseWellFormedV3SuccessIsMismatch`\n204|  and `TestDecodeResponseV3FailureWithValid130ErrorIsMismatch` — the latter\n205|  first decodes the embedded error through the production `(provider, 3)` ->\n206|  1.3.0 binding, so refusal is of a genuinely well-formed foreign error.\n207|  `TestDecodeResponseV2FailureWith130ErrorIsBoundTo100` pins that the contract\n208|  is selected by the observed major, not the document.\n209|- **The lift seam**: `Lift` builds the wire message from the stable code alone,\n210|  Details empty, cause local-only; four production-derived vectors (real\n211|  `Discover`/`Verify` refusals) assert the secrets are present in `Error()` and\n212|  absent from the marshalled wire object — a measured removal, not a vacuous\n213|  non-mention. `TestNaiveLiftShapeIsRefusedByTheWireGate` refuses the naive\n214|  shape in both the message and the details direction.\n215|  `TestLiftRefusesRegisteredCodeWithoutLiftArm` pins the fail-closed default\n216|  arm and discriminates it from the unregistered-code arm.\n217|- **N6 closed**: the CallExpr-only bound now sits on\n218|  `TestNoProductionPathAttestsProviderIdentityBinding`'s doc comment.\n219|- **AC rows 1–13 and 15** re-run green in the full suite; row 14 remains a\n220|  declared stated bound (14 driven + 1 bound, honestly reported).\n221|\n222|## Notes (non-blocking)\n223|\n224|- **N7 carried**: the §7.A deferral still names no follow-up board item. Per the\n225|  round-4 brief this is the orchestrator's board-element freeze, not a producer\n226|  omission.\n227|- **N8**: `AdmitProviderDescriptor` still has zero production callers, disclosed\n228|  in its own doc comment with the intended call order. Systemic and honest;\n229|  restated so it is not lost.\n230|- **N9**: D3 (`+`) is an equivalent mutant by reachability. Worth one declared\n231|  line in the census rather than a test row.\n232|\n233|## Reviewer battery\n234|\n235|14 mutants, all applied to a scratch copy and restored byte-identically.\n236|11 KILLED / 3 SURVIVED (D1, D2, S1 — the two blocking findings; D3 declared\n237|equivalent). Full rows: `TASK-260906-vmzk0y_review-rev4-battery.json`, harness\n238|`TASK-260906-vmzk0y_review-rev4-battery.py`."}}}
