{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c745","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07939-d4d2-7553-8d6d-07967bfdd55f"},"sequence":509,"recorded_at":1780531400001013,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"9ce0545c-46a3-414d-a8ed-c43a478642c3","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"9ce0545c-46a3-414d-a8ed-c43a478642c3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"9ce0545c-46a3-414d-a8ed-c43a478642c3"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"6026bade-7b54-4965-be62-7e22fa988b65"},"task_id":"6026bade-7b54-4965-be62-7e22fa988b65","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"6026bade-7b54-4965-be62-7e22fa988b65","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260906-vmzk0y/TASK-260906-vmzk0y_outcome-round4.md`.\n1|# TASK-260906-vmzk0y — own-provider-protocol-v3-envelope-and-error-lift (round 4)\n2|\n3|Status: ready for review (handed off to review; board status `to-review`).\n4|\n5|Candidate tree: `6c8e29de0765747dc93c8565a756a888c6609ca6`\n6|(verified by `git ls-tree -r`: all four new files\n7|`internal/provider/lift.go`, `internal/provider/lift_test.go`,\n8|`internal/terminalbackend/descriptor.go`,\n9|`internal/terminalbackend/descriptor_test.go` are in-tree; `git hash-object`\n10|of the worktree `protocol.go`, `protocol_test.go`, `identity_test.go`, and\n11|`LOGBOOK.md` byte-for-byte equals the tree blobs. Built via a detached index —\n12|`GIT_INDEX_FILE` copy + `read-tree HEAD` + `add -A` + `write-tree` — so the\n13|worktree index is untouched.)\n14|\n15|Round 4 answers review-verdict-rev3: one blocking finding (F1a saturation-edge\n16|+ F1b digit-range token-preserving, second consecutive round of the same\n17|class) plus notes N4–N7. Everything else stands exactly as the reviewer\n18|verified it — G-A (malformed giants pinned apart, migration reddens, peek\n19|divergence gone on bare and full frames), G-B (round-2 sentence withdrawn as\n20|classification evidence), G-C (N1/N3 closed), G-D battery denominator, F1/F2/F4/F5\n21|classes, F3 bound, §7.A ownership, Lift fail-closed arms, (provider,3)→1.3.0\n22|binding — and is not re-litigated here. No production change in round 4: the\n23|`parseMajor` guard was already correct; the delta is three behavioural test\n24|groups plus the N6 doc sentence.\n25|\n26|## F1a (blocking, closed) — saturation guard pinned at its edge\n27|\n28|The guard `major > (math.MaxInt-step)/10` was witnessed only far above its\n29|edge (2^64+1, 2^64+2, 2^64, 41 nines), where saturation is sticky. The true\n30|narrowing `major > math.MaxInt/10` (drops the `step` term) differs only when\n31|the accumulator sits at exactly MaxInt/10 (922337203685477580) and the next\n32|digit is 8 or 9. New `TestParseMajorSaturationEdge` drives five rows through\n33|the production entry point `DecodeResponse`, each requiring parseMajor ==\n34|MaxInt (not merely recognized), major != 2, and\n35|`incompatible_protocol` / exit 6 with `observed` echoed:\n36|\n37|| `protocol_version` | shipped | under M3 (`> MaxInt/10`) |\n38||---|---|---|\n39|| `9223372036854775807.0.0` (MaxInt, largest admitted) | (MaxInt,true) → 6 | identical (no saturation on the exact fit) |\n40|| `9223372036854775808.0.0` (MaxInt+1, first saturated) | (MaxInt,true) → 6 | (-9223372036854775808,true) → 6 (exit same, parse value kills) |\n41|| `922337203685477580801.0.0` (aliasing neighbour, wraps to 1) | (MaxInt,true) → 6 | (1,true) → 6 (exit same, parse value kills) |\n42|| `922337203685477580802.0.0` (aliasing witness, wraps to 2) | (MaxInt,true) → 6 | (2,true) → `provider_protocol_error` exit 13 |\n43|| `922337203685477580803.0.0` (aliasing neighbour, wraps to 3) | (MaxInt,true) → 6 | (3,true) → 6 (exit same, parse value kills) |\n44|\n45|The witness construction: `922337203685477580` walks the accumulator to\n46|exactly MaxInt/10; the next `8` overflows int64 to -2^63; the following `0`\n47|multiplies by 10 (0 mod 2^64), resetting to 0; the final `2` lands on 2 — a\n48|foreign major aliasing native major 2, verbatim the invariant the `parseMajor`\n49|doc comment asserts. The ±1 neighbours pin the fix at the guard, not a\n50|literal blocklist of one string. Measured: M3 is KILLED by\n51|`TestParseMajorSaturationEdge` alone\n52|(`parseMajor(\"9223372036854775808.0.0\") = -9223372036854775808, want\n53|saturation to math.MaxInt`); `go test ./internal/provhost/ -count=1` passes on\n54|shipped code.\n55|\n56|## F1b (blocking, closed) — digit-range arms pinned behaviourally at `/` and `:`\n57|\n58|The major arm computes `digit < '0' || digit > '9'` and the rest arm computes\n59|`rest[i] < '0' || rest[i] > '9'`. The corpus used `a`, `2a`, `-1`, `+3`, `b`,\n60|`c` — never the two characters adjacent to the range: `/` (0x2F, one below\n61|`'0'`) and `:` (0x3A, one above `'9'`). New\n62|`TestParseMajorDigitBoundariesRefuseAtEntry` drives eight rows through\n63|`DecodeResponse`, each requiring parseMajor unrecognized AND\n64|`provider_protocol_error` / exit 13 with member `protocol_version` /\n65|`unsupported protocol version`:\n66|\n67|`3/.0.0`, `/.0.0` (`/` in major) · `3:.0.0`, `:.0.0` (`:` in major) ·\n68|`3./.0`, `3.0./` (`/` in minor, patch) · `3.:.0`, `3.0.:` (`:` in minor, patch)\n69|\n70|— so `/` and `:` are covered in the major and in each rest position, plus the\n71|leading single-character majors, verifying one step away from any single\n72|finding vector. Measured effect of the token-preserving inserts (condition\n73|text unchanged, derived arm set byte-identical, bijection stays 167/167):\n74|\n75|| mutant (production edit, condition text preserved) | shipped | under mutant |\n76||---|---|---|\n77|| M17 `if digit == ':' { continue }` above the major check | (0,false) → 13 | (3,true) → 6 |\n78|| M17b `if digit == '/' { continue }` above the major check | (0,false) → 13 | (3,true) → 6 |\n79|| M18 `if rest[i] == '/' { continue }` above the rest check | (0,false) → 13 | (3,true) → 6 |\n80|| M18b `if rest[i] == ':' { continue }` above the rest check | (0,false) → 13 | (3,true) → 6 |\n81|\n82|All four are KILLED by `TestParseMajorDigitBoundariesRefuseAtEntry` with zero\n83|census kill (the census cannot see them by construction). The same rows give\n84|the condition-editing narrowings their first behavioural killers: M5\n85|(`rest[i] < '/'`), M5b (`rest[i] > ':'`), M6 (`digit > ':'`), M6b\n86|(`digit < '/'`) are now killed by the new behavioural test IN ADDITION to the\n87|inventory bijection (previously census-only).\n88|\n89|## Round-4 mutation battery (F1 gate)\n90|\n91|Denominator re-derived for this revision from production: the nine\n92|version-classification obligations reachable from `DecodeResponse` — P1\n93|`len(parts) != 3`, P2 major-digit range, P3 saturation guard, P4\n94|`len(parts[0]) == 0`, P5 `len(rest) == 0`, P6 rest-digit range, C1\n95|failure-error contract major selection, K1 `foreignMajor` peek predicate, V1\n96|version-gate mismatch predicate. Battery script\n97|`.temp/TASK-260906-vmzk0y/mut_round4.py` (evidence\n98|`.temp/TASK-260906-vmzk0y/battery-round4-all.json`, per-subset files\n99|`battery-round4-*.json`); every `go test ./internal/provhost/ -count=1` ran as\n100|a standalone process with its real exit code preserved (no pipe chain), and\n101|each target file was restored byte-identically afterwards (SHA-256 asserted,\n102|`ALL RESTORED`).\n103|\n104|Applied 22 / killed 21 / survived 1 (declared equivalent, see bound below).\n105|Controls NOT_APPLIED and COMPILE_FAIL are distinct rows, not counted as\n106|applied. Killer split: BEHAVIOURAL = drives a production entry point\n107|(`DecodeResponse`, `EncodeRequest`, `Host.Call`, `DecodeBound` wrappers);\n108|CENSUS = source-text inventory only\n109|(`TestDerivedRefusalArmsAreAllWitnessed`, `TestWitnessedArmsAreAllDerived`).\n110|`TestEveryArmWitnessRefusesAtTheProductionEntry` drives the entry, so it\n111|counts as behavioural.\n112|\n113|| Mutant | What it narrows the gate to | Named test(s) that fail | Behavioural killer? |\n114||---|---|---|---|\n115|| M1 narrowing (P3): saturation `continue` back to early `return MaxInt, true` | giant-with-malformed-rest reads recognized (exit 6, not 13) | `TestParseMajorSaturationStillValidatesTheRest`, `TestDecodeResponseUnrecognizedVersionRunsMemberRules` | BEHAVIOURAL (no census) |\n116|| M2 narrowing (P3): guard neutered to `major > math.MaxInt` (never fires) | accumulation wraps again | `TestParseMajorNeverWraps`, `TestParseMajorSaturationEdge` | BEHAVIOURAL (no census) |\n117|| M3 TRUE NARROWING (P3): `major > (MaxInt-step)/10` → `major > MaxInt/10` | threshold off by one; `...802` aliases native 2 | `TestParseMajorSaturationEdge` | BEHAVIOURAL (no census) |\n118|| M4 narrowing (P5): `len(rest) == 0` → `len(rest) < 0` (never fires) | empty rest admitted | `TestDecodeResponseRefusals` + subrow, `TestEveryArmWitness.../empty_minor`, `TestParseMajorSaturationStillValidatesTheRest` + census pair | BOTH |\n119|| M5 narrowing (P6 condition-edit): `rest[i] < '/'` | rest admits exactly `/` | `TestParseMajorDigitBoundariesRefuseAtEntry` (new) + census pair | BOTH (was census-only) |\n120|| M5b narrowing (P6 condition-edit mirror): `rest[i] > ':'` | rest admits exactly `:` | same as M5 | BOTH |\n121|| M6 narrowing (P2 condition-edit): `digit > ':'` | major admits exactly `:` | `TestParseMajorDigitBoundariesRefuseAtEntry` (new) + census pair | BOTH (was census-only) |\n122|| M6b narrowing (P2 condition-edit mirror): `digit < '/'` | major admits exactly `/` | same as M6 | BOTH |\n123|| M7 narrowing (P1): `len(parts) != 3` → `len(parts) < 3` | over-long shape (4+ parts) admitted | `TestDecodeResponseRefusals` + subrow + census pair | BOTH |\n124|| M8 narrowing (P4): `len(parts[0]) == 0` → `< 0` (never fires) | empty major admitted | `TestDecodeResponseRefusals` + subrow, `TestEveryArmWitness.../empty_major` + census pair | BOTH |\n125|| M11 narrowing (C1): contract `observedMajor` → `observedMajor+1` | failure-error contract off the observed major | `TestDecodeResponseV2FailureWith130ErrorIsBoundTo100`, `TestDecodeResponseReturnsChildFailure`, `TestChildFailureCodesPassThrough*` | BEHAVIOURAL (no census) |\n126|| M13b narrowing (K1): peek `recognized && ...` → `recognized \\|\\| ...` (widen) | unrecognized versions skip member rules (N4) | `TestDecodeResponseUnrecognizedVersionRunsMemberRules` (new) | BEHAVIOURAL (no census; was SURVIVED) |\n127|| M14b narrowing (K1): peek `!= ProtocolMajor` → `> ProtocolMajor` | major 1 no longer a mismatch | `TestDecodeResponseForeignMajorPrecedesMemberRules` + subrow | BEHAVIOURAL (no census) |\n128|| M16 narrowing (V1): gate `!= ProtocolMajor` → `> ProtocolMajor` | major 1 falls to unsupported-version | `TestDecodeResponseForeignMajorPrecedesMemberRules` + subrow, `TestDecodeResponseRecognizableMajorMismatch` | BEHAVIOURAL (no census) |\n129|| M17 narrowing/token-preserving (P2): insert `if digit == ':' { continue }` | major admits exactly `:`; census byte-identical | `TestParseMajorDigitBoundariesRefuseAtEntry` | BEHAVIOURAL ONLY (zero census kill — the point) |\n130|| M17b narrowing/token-preserving (P2): insert `if digit == '/' { continue }` | major admits exactly `/`; census byte-identical | same | BEHAVIOURAL ONLY |\n131|| M18 narrowing/token-preserving (P6): insert `if rest[i] == '/' { continue }` | rest admits exactly `/`; census byte-identical | same | BEHAVIOURAL ONLY |\n132|| M18b narrowing/token-preserving (P6): insert `if rest[i] == ':' { continue }` | rest admits exactly `:`; census byte-identical | same | BEHAVIOURAL ONLY |\n133|| M9 arm-deletion (P5+P6): whole minor/patch validation deleted | every malformed rest admitted | `TestDecodeResponseRefusals` + subrows, `TestEveryArmWitness...` + new boundary test + census pair | BOTH |\n134|| M10 arm-deletion (P1): three-part shape check deleted | 2-part and 4-part admitted | `TestDecodeResponseRefusals` + subrows, `TestEveryArmWitness...` | BOTH (census pair co-fires via TestWitnessedArms... — counted in full list) |\n135|| M15 census-only: census derives zero parse arms (production untouched) | inventory must orphan declared parse witnesses | `TestDerivedRefusalArmsAreAllWitnessed`, `TestWitnessedArmsAreAllDerived` | CENSUS ONLY (mutates the census itself) |\n136|| M12 equivalence-probe (C1): contract back to hardcoded `Major: 2` | no observable change (only 2.0.0 reaches the line) | SURVIVES — declared equivalent, bound N5 | survivor bound stated below |\n137|\n138|Class split: narrowing 14/14 killed (incl. the true P3 narrowing M3);\n139|narrowing/token-preserving 4/4 killed, all behaviourally with zero census\n140|kill; arm-deletion 2/2 killed; census-only 1/1 killed; equivalence-probe 0/1\n141|(declared equivalent). No surviving mutant except M12.\n142|\n143|Distinct control rows, NOT counted as applied mutants:\n144|\n145|| Control | Disposition |\n146||---|---|\n147|| X1: anchor with `>=` absent from source (0 sites) | NOT_APPLIED |\n148|| X2: guard deleted outright (`math` import unused) | COMPILE_FAIL |\n149|\n150|Survival bound: M12 survives because only `2.0.0` reaches the failure-error\n151|contract line today (the version gate refuses every other version above), so\n152|`Major: observedMajor` and `Major: 2` coincide on every reachable path; the\n153|`protocol.go` comment states exactly this, and shifting the major OFF the\n154|observed value (M11) is killed by eight tests. Recorded per N5 so it is not\n155|mistaken for a hole later.\n156|\n157|Per-arm behavioural-vs-census verdict: every production arm except the\n158|census-itself probe M15 now carries at least one BEHAVIOURAL killer. Arms\n159|whose only killers were the census pair in rev3 (P2/P6 condition-edits M5/M6)\n160|now carry the new behavioural test alongside the census pair; the four\n161|token-preserving narrowings carry a behavioural killer and explicitly no\n162|census kill, which is what proves the inventory is blind to that shape.\n163|\n164|## Notes N4–N7\n165|\n166|- N4 (peek widening, FIXED not merely confirmed): M13b survived rev3 with a\n167|  member-detail slide (`ok` → `protocol_version`) on bare frames, code and\n168|  exit unchanged. New `TestDecodeResponseUnrecognizedVersionRunsMemberRules`\n169|  pins the narrowing direction behaviourally (bare frame with `2.abc.def` and\n170|  `99999999999999999999.abc.def` must report member `ok` / `missing member`),\n171|  so M13b is now KILLED by that test alone. The narrowing direction was\n172|  already killed (M14b); both directions are now behaviourally pinned.\n173|- N5: M12 is the declared equivalent above, not a hole; M11 kills the\n174|  off-observed shift.\n175|- N6: the N2 CallExpr-only bound now lives on the test's doc comment\n176|  (`TestNoProductionPathAttestsProviderIdentityBinding` carries the `f :=\n177|  pkg.VerifyObjectIdentity; f(x)` sentence), not only in the outcome.\n178|- N7: carried since rev2 and accepted there — the §7.A deferral loop names no\n179|  follow-up board item; per the round-4 brief that attachment is the\n180|  orchestrator's board-element freeze, not this leaf's.\n181|\n182|## AC row coverage: 14 of 15 driven + 1 stated bound (N1, carried)\n183|\n184|Rows 1–13 and 15 were driven through the production entry point by the named\n185|test in rounds 1–3 and re-run green in this round's full suite; row 14 (F6,\n186|future caller recorded) is prose by nature and stays a stated bound. Round 4\n187|adds the F1a/F1b/N4 behavioural rows to row 6 and the N6 sentence to row 12;\n188|no other row changes.\n189|\n190|| # | AC / DoD row | Production call site | Driving test / bound |\n191||---|---|---|---|\n192|| 1 | v3 envelope has exactly one named owner, recorded in provhost stated bounds and the ownership registry | `internal/provhost/doc.go`, `ownership.v0.5.0.json` `section:7.A` | `tracecheck`: ok (60 contracts, 98 cases) |\n193|| 2 | working v3 admission or explicit stated bound naming the deferral | `terminalbackend.AdmitProviderDescriptor`; `provhost/doc.go` | `TestAdmitProviderDescriptorAdmitsMatchingBinding`, `TestAdmitProviderDescriptorRefusesMismatch` |\n194|| 3 | v3 envelope reaching provhost → documented outcome, both directions | `provhost.DecodeResponse`; `terminalbackend.AdmitProviderDescriptor` | `TestDecodeResponseWellFormedV3SuccessIsMismatch`, `TestDecodeResponseV3FailureWithValid130ErrorIsMismatch` |\n195|| 4 | Error 1.3.0 binding implemented-or-deferred; no silent major-2 binding for v3 | `provhost.DecodeResponse` (observed-major contract), `axerror.BindingFor`/`DecodeBound` | `TestDecodeResponseV2FailureWith130ErrorIsBoundTo100`; the v3 test decodes its embedded error through production `(provider, 3)` → 1.3.0 |\n196|| 5 | F1: geometry bound decided on digits, overflow refused | `terminalbackend.descriptorGeometry` | `TestParseProviderDescriptorGeometryOverflowVectors` |\n197|| 6 | F2+G1+F1a+F1b+N4: majors never wrap; saturation validates the full shape; guard edge and digit edges pinned; peek directions pinned | `terminalbackend.semverMajor`, `provhost.parseMajor` + `DecodeResponse` | `TestParseProviderDescriptorProtocolVersionOverflowVectors`, `TestParseMajorNeverWraps` (exit-6), `TestParseMajorSaturationStillValidatesTheRest` (exit-13), NEW `TestParseMajorSaturationEdge` (M3), NEW `TestParseMajorDigitBoundariesRefuseAtEntry` (M5/M6/M17/M18 + mirrors), NEW `TestDecodeResponseUnrecognizedVersionRunsMemberRules` (M13b) |\n198|| 7 | F4: registered-but-unlifted code produces no wire object | `provider.Lift` | `TestLiftRefusesRegisteredCodeWithoutLiftArm`, `TestLiftRefusesUnregisteredCode` |\n199|| 8 | discovery failure lifts into an axerror Structured Error through an accepted production path | `provider.Lift` | `TestLiftCarriesDiscoveryFailuresToTheWire` |\n200|| 9 | causal-leak shape refused (negative) | `axerror.New` | `TestNaiveLiftShapeIsRefusedByTheWireGate` |\n201|| 10 | no machine-local path, provider ID, or owner identity on any wire message | `provider.Lift`, `terminalbackend` parse arms | wire-absence asserts in all 4 lift vectors; `TestParseProviderDescriptorRefusesWithoutEchoingLocalData` |\n202|| 11 | CheckProviderDescriptor completed; registry owns 7.A | `terminalbackend.ParseProviderDescriptor` + `AdmitProviderDescriptor`; registry | 12 inventory arms + rows (bijection 210/210); `tracecheck` ok |\n203|| 12 | F3: bound rests on true facts, both halves pinned | `provhost/identity.go` header | `TestSpecIdentityExampleVerifiesAgainstItsClaimedDigest`, `TestNoProductionPathAttestsProviderIdentityBinding` (0 production call sites; N2 bound now on the test) |\n204|| 13 | F5: census derives the whole package, every form, fail-closed | `loadProviderCodes` | `TestLiftCoversTheClosedCodeSet` + var/grouped/fail-closed plants |\n205|| 14 | F6: future caller recorded | `terminalbackend/descriptor.go` | STATED BOUND (prose by nature; names path, order, two miswirings); the gate it will guard is driven by row 2 |\n206|| 15 | mutation battery with narrowing / arm-deletion / census-only split | `.temp/TASK-260906-vmzk0y/mut_round4.py` | this round: 22 applied / 21 killed / 1 survived-equivalent + NOT_APPLIED + COMPILE_FAIL distinct; prior batteries stand |\n207|\n208|## Production changes in round 4 (no production change)\n209|\n210|- `internal/provhost/protocol_test.go`: three new behavioural tests\n211|  (`TestParseMajorSaturationEdge`, `TestParseMajorDigitBoundariesRefuseAtEntry`,\n212|  `TestDecodeResponseUnrecognizedVersionRunsMemberRules`) + `math` import.\n213|- `internal/provhost/identity_test.go`: N2 stated bound moved onto the\n214|  tripwire's doc comment (N6).\n215|- `LOGBOOK.md`: entry 2253 (this round).\n216|- All other round-1/2/3 paths byte-identical; leaf-1 packages untouched\n217|  (`git diff --name-only 1d97474 -- internal/canonicaljson internal/environ\n218|  internal/terminalbackend/manifest.go` returns 0 files — re-verified this\n219|  round). Same 15 paths (11 modified + 4 new) as rev3.\n220|\n221|## Gates re-run by this round (nothing accepted from prior rounds)\n222|\n223|| Gate | Result |\n224||---|---|\n225|| `go build ./...` | exit 0 |\n226|| `go vet ./...` | exit 0 |\n227|| `go test ./... -count=1` | exit 0, 22 packages ok, no FAIL |\n228|| `go test ./internal/provider/ ./internal/provhost/ ./internal/terminalbackend/ -cover -count=1` | exit 0 — 97.8% / 85.8% / 94.2% |\n229|| `gofmt -l internal/` | clean |\n230|| `go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck` | ok — contracts=60, acceptance_cases=98 |\n231|| provhost refusal-arm bijection | 167/167 derived arms witnessed |\n232|\n233|Not run in this round (stated, not implied): `GOOS=windows go build/vet` and\n234|`go test -race` were green in rev3 and are unchanged by this test-only delta;\n235|they were not re-run here for time. No gate is claimed on their behalf."}}}
