utant battery with behavioural-vs-census split per arm, candidate tree OID verified by `ls-tree`); battery script `mut_round4.py` + `battery-round4-all.json` under repo-root `.temp/TASK-260906-vmzk0y/`.\\n18:- SCOPE: TASK-260906-vmzk0y rework (G1 blocking + N1–N3 notes; F1/F2/F4/F5 and the F3 rewrite stand as the reviewer verified them and were not re-litigated). Production: `provhost/protocol.go` `parseMajor` only — the saturating early `return math.MaxInt, true` is now `major = math.MaxInt; continue`, so an overflowing first component still saturates but the minor/patch shape check always runs. Doc paragraph narrowed to what the code enforces (only a fully numeric X.Y.Z reports a recognized major). Tests: new `TestParseMajorSaturationStillValidatesTheRest` (5 giant-malformed rows assert `parseMajor` unrecognized AND `DecodeResponse` provider_protocol_error/exit 13 through the production entry).\\n20:- CORRECTION: the round-2 outcome sentence \\\"no gate was weakened … parse-arm census derives the identical set\\\" is withdrawn as classification-stability evidence in `TASK-260906-vmzk0y_outcome-round3.md`; the census claim survives only in its scoped form (saturation adds no `return 0, false` branch, so the inventory needs no new row). AC ratio corrected to 14 of 15 driven + 1 stated bound (row 14, F6 future-caller prose). N2 bound stated: the attestation tripwire matches `CallExpr` only, so a function-value binding would be missed (0 such references today). Battery scripts live at repo-root `.temp/TASK-260906-vmzk0y/` (N3).\\n21:- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260906-vmzk0y_outcome-round3.md` on the board task (G1 table, corrected arm-shift sentence, 14+1 AC ratio, 8-mutant battery table); battery script `mutG1_round3.py` + `mutsG1_round3.json` under repo-root `.temp/TASK-260906-vmzk0y/`.\\n27:- SCOPE: TASK-260906-vmzk0y rework (F1–F5 blocking, F6–F7 notes). Production: `terminalbackend/descriptor.go` (early bound refusal in `descriptorGeometry`), `terminalbackend.go` (`semverMajor` saturates), `provhost/protocol.go` (`parseMajor` saturates, no new census branch), `provider/lift.go` (default arm fail-closed: unregistered → registry refusal, registered-no-arm → input handed back, never a wire object). Docs: provhost `doc.go`/`identity.go` bounds rewritten, descriptor future-caller paragraph. Tests: overflow vectors (F1/F2), registered-no-arm refusal (F4), §5.5 verify measurement + attestation tripwire (F3), whole-package multi-form derivation + 4 plants (F5), v3-error DecodeBound premise proof.\\n31:- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260906-vmzk0y_outcome.md` updated on the board task (15/15 AC rows with call sites; battery 26 applied / 26 killed / 0 survivors + NOT_APPLIED and COMPILE_FAIL controls as distinct rows; candidate tree OID verified by `ls-tree`).\\n36:- SCOPE: TASK-260906-vmzk0y (second leaf of STORY-260905-3t31e9; advisories A3/A4 + carried F3). New: `terminalbackend/descriptor.go` (closed §7.A descriptor parse + `AdmitProviderDescriptor`), `provider/lift.go` (`Lift`); edited: provhost protocol/doc/identity comments + derived error contract, provider doc, 7.A registry group + digest, terminalbackend inventory rows. Leaf-1 production untouched.\\n40:- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260906-vmzk0y_outcome.md` on the board task (11/11 AC rows with call sites, 19-row mutant table, gates with exit codes, candidate tree OID verified by `ls-tree`).\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 4408,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1102,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
