{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000ce2d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07939-d4d2-7553-8d6d-07967bfdd55f"},"sequence":1393,"recorded_at":1780531400002781,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"9ce0545c-46a3-414d-a8ed-c43a478642c3","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"9ce0545c-46a3-414d-a8ed-c43a478642c3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"9ce0545c-46a3-414d-a8ed-c43a478642c3"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"318d86bb-10d2-4af2-bdbc-ac39b763acf0"},"task_id":"318d86bb-10d2-4af2-bdbc-ac39b763acf0","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"318d86bb-10d2-4af2-bdbc-ac39b763acf0","chunk":"Read text file `LOGBOOK.md`.\n1|# Flight Logbook\n2|\n3|> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\n4|> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\n5|\n6|## 2026-09-06\n7|\n8|### 2253 — review round 4: parse-gate edges pinned behaviourally, census-only kills closed (F1a/F1b)\n9|\n10|- SCOPE: TASK-260906-vmzk0y rework (F1a saturation-edge + F1b digit-range token-preserving, N4 peek-widening, N6 test-bound placement). No production change: `provhost/protocol.go` guard was already correct. Tests: new `TestParseMajorSaturationEdge` (MaxInt, MaxInt+1, aliasing witness 922337203685477580802.0.0 ±1, each requiring parseMajor==MaxInt AND DecodeResponse incompatible_protocol/exit 6), new `TestParseMajorDigitBoundariesRefuseAtEntry` ('/' 0x2F and ':' 0x3A in major and in each rest position, each requiring parseMajor unrecognized AND DecodeResponse provider_protocol_error/exit 13), new `TestDecodeResponseUnrecognizedVersionRunsMemberRules` (bare-frame member `ok` pins the peek widening). Doc: N2 CallExpr-only bound moved onto `TestNoProductionPathAttestsProviderIdentityBinding` (N6).\n11|- FINDING (measured): weakened guard `major > math.MaxInt/10` wraps 922337203685477580802.0.0 to major 2 (exit 13, aliasing native 2) while shipped saturates to MaxInt (exit 6); token-preserving inserts (`if digit == ':' { continue }`, `if rest[i] == '/' { continue }`, plus the '/' -in-major and ':'-in-rest mirrors) leave the derived arm set byte-identical (bijection 167/167) and survived the whole suite; peek widening `recognized || ...` slides bare-frame member `ok` to `protocol_version` with code/exit unchanged. All now redden behaviourally.\n12|- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260906-vmzk0y_outcome-round4.md` on the board task (F1a/F1b tables, 22-mutant battery with behavioural-vs-census split per arm, candidate tree OID verified by `ls-tree`); battery script `mut_round4.py` + `battery-round4-all.json` under repo-root `.temp/TASK-260906-vmzk0y/`.\n13|- GATES: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (22 pkgs), `-cover` exit 0 (provider 97.8%, provhost 85.8%, terminalbackend 94.2%), `go vet` exit 0, `go build` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` ok (60 contracts, 98 acceptance cases). Battery: 22 applied / 21 killed / 1 survived (M12 declared equivalent per N5) + NOT_APPLIED and COMPILE_FAIL as distinct control rows; all 4 token-preserving killed behaviourally with zero census kill.\n14|- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off to review (review/integration are orchestrator steps).\n15|\n16|### 2252 — review round 3: saturation short-circuit reclassified malformed versions (G1)\n17|\n18|- SCOPE: TASK-260906-vmzk0y rework (G1 blocking + N1–N3 notes; F1/F2/F4/F5 and the F3 rewrite stand as the reviewer verified them and were not re-litigated). Production: `provhost/protocol.go` `parseMajor` only — the saturating early `return math.MaxInt, true` is now `major = math.MaxInt; continue`, so an overflowing first component still saturates but the minor/patch shape check always runs. Doc paragraph narrowed to what the code enforces (only a fully numeric X.Y.Z reports a recognized major). Tests: new `TestParseMajorSaturationStillValidatesTheRest` (5 giant-malformed rows assert `parseMajor` unrecognized AND `DecodeResponse` provider_protocol_error/exit 13 through the production entry).\n(more lines below)"}}}
