set byte-identical (bijection 167/167) and survived the whole suite; peek widening `recognized || ...` slides bare-frame member `ok` to `protocol_version` with code/exit unchanged. All now redden behaviourally.\n12|- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260906-vmzk0y_outcome-round4.md` on the board task (F1a/F1b tables, 22-mutant battery with behavioural-vs-census split per arm, candidate tree OID verified by `ls-tree`); battery script `mut_round4.py` + `battery-round4-all.json` under repo-root `.temp/TASK-260906-vmzk0y/`.\n13|- GATES: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (22 pkgs), `-cover` exit 0 (provider 97.8%, provhost 85.8%, terminalbackend 94.2%), `go vet` exit 0, `go build` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` ok (60 contracts, 98 acceptance cases). Battery: 22 applied / 21 killed / 1 survived (M12 declared equivalent per N5) + NOT_APPLIED and COMPILE_FAIL as distinct control rows; all 4 token-preserving killed behaviourally with zero census kill.\n14|- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off to review (review/integration are orchestrator steps).\n15|\n16|### 2252 — review round 3: saturation short-circuit reclassified malformed versions (G1)\n17|\n18|- SCOPE: TASK-260906-vmzk0y rework (G1 blocking + N1–N3 notes; F1/F2/F4/F5 and the F3 rewrite stand as the reviewer verified them and were not re-litigated). Production: `provhost/protocol.go` `parseMajor` only — the saturating early `return math.MaxInt, true` is now `major = math.MaxInt; continue`, so an overflowing first component still saturates but the minor/patch shape check always runs. Doc paragraph narrowed to what the code enforces (only a fully numeric X.Y.Z reports a recognized major). Tests: new `TestParseMajorSaturationStillValidatesTheRest` (5 giant-malformed rows assert `parseMajor` unrecognized AND `DecodeResponse` provider_protocol_error/exit 13 through the production entry).\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
