3685477580801.0.0 at ParseProviderDescriptor with err=nil (semverMajor returns 1, aliasing native major 1); weakened bound `digit > 'E'` admits `columns: 1E2` as Columns=312; both survived the whole 457-test suite. The neighbours refuse either way, so the value pins (==MaxInt) carry those kills — the round-4 lesson, re-applied. `+` is a declared equivalent (only legal after e/E, which refuses first); `/` and `:` are provably unreachable through json.Number.\n+- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260906-vmzk0y_outcome-round5.md` on the board task (F1/F2 tables, 9-mutant battery with behavioural-vs-census split per arm, candidate tree OID verified by `ls-tree`); harness `TASK-260906-vmzk0y_mut-round5.py` + `TASK-260906-vmzk0y_battery-round5.json` attached as task resources.\n+- GATES: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (22 pkgs, 0 FAIL), `-cover` exit 0 (provider 97.8%, provhost 85.8%, terminalbackend 94.2%), `go vet` exit 0, `go build` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` ok (60 contracts, 36 sections, 98 cases), `GOOS=windows go build/vet` exit 0, `-race` exit 0 on provhost + terminalbackend. Battery: 9 applied / 8 killed / 1 survived (T-D3 `+`, declared equivalent) + NOT_APPLIED and COMPILE_FAIL as distinct control rows; all 3 token-preserving killed-or-equivalent with zero census kill except the arm-deletion, which co-fires the census pair by construction.\n+- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off to review (review/integration are orchestrator steps).\n+\n+### 2253 — review round 4: parse-gate edges pinned behaviourally, census-only kills closed (F1a/F1b)\n"}}}
